=== files --help ===

Commands:
  download  Download a file from HopsFS to the local filesystem.
  list      List files under ``path`` in the project's HopsFS.
  mkdir     Create a directory in the project's HopsFS.
  remove    Remove a file or directory from HopsFS.
  share     Share a dataset with another project.
  unshare   Revoke a previously-granted dataset share with another project.
  upload    Upload a local file to HopsFS.
=== model register --help ===
Usage: hops model register [OPTIONS] NAME PATH

  Upload a trained model artifact to the Hopsworks model registry.

  Args:     ctx: Click context.     name: Model name.     path: Local path to
  the model artifact (file or directory).     framework: ML framework category
  (``sklearn``/``tensorflow``/``torch``/``python``/``llm``).     metrics_spec:
  Metrics as ``key=value`` pairs.     description: Description string.
  feature_view: Feature view the model was trained on.     td_version:
  Training dataset version used for training.     input_example_path: JSON
  file holding a representative input.     version: Explicit model version.

Options:
  --framework [keras|llm|python|pytorch|scikit-learn|sklearn|tensorflow|tf|torch]
                                  ML framework category.  [default: python]
  --metrics TEXT                  Comma-separated metrics, e.g.
                                  "accuracy=0.95,auc=0.91".
  --description TEXT              Model description.
  --feature-view TEXT             Feature view used for training.
  --td-version INTEGER            Training dataset version used for training.
  --input-example PATH            JSON file with a r
